`c_5` value (no closure yet — empirical is ≈ -395.4\nat q_0, well off any simple multi-link Jones combination). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MultiLinkJonesAtOne.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MultiLinkJonesAtOne.mk","kind":"ctor","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L93-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.MultiLinkJonesAtOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.MultiLinkJonesAtOne","kind":"class","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L90-L99","doc":"**Multi-link Jones c_5 / c_6 candidate class.** Records the\nspecific scalar values a downstream theorem can plug in for\n`c_5, c_6` in the precision ladder extension. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesDoubleHopfValue_eq_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesDoubleHopfValue_eq_four","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L80-L81","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesDoubleHopfValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesDoubleHopfValue","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L76-L78","doc":"`J_DoubleHopf = 4`. Candidate for c_5 under double-Hopf disjoint-\nunion hypothesis. Also empirically far off (`-395` vs `4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesBorromeanFlipped_eq_eight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesBorromeanFlipped_eq_eight","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L73-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesBorromeanFlipped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesBorromeanFlipped","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L67-L71","doc":"`J_Borromean (sign-flipped) = +8`. The probe found this as the\nbest simple-integer candidate for c_5, but the empirical value\nis `≈ -395.4` — a 50× mismatch in scale. Reported here for\ncompleteness; does NOT match empirical. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfTimesBorromean_eq_sixteen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfTimesBorromean_eq_sixteen","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L63-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfTimesBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopfTimesBorromean","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/multi-link-jones-q1-extension.lean#L59-L61","doc":"`J_Hopf · J_Borromean = (-2) · (-8) = 16`. Candidate for c_6\nunder the disjoint-union-multiplicativity hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0}]}